{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>This one fellow came to sojourn and would judge judge.</b> Behold, on that very day they appointed him judge over them, as Rashi explained; so why did they rage against him? The correct explanation is as the commentators expounded on the doubled expression 'וַיִּשְׁפֹּט שָׁפוֹט' — you wish to judge a matter that has already been judged, for he had already established for them a statute and ordinance that no traveler shall enter the dwelling of any individual; and how do you wish to change the statute already decided? For according to that understanding we did not accept you in order to make new statutes. And what they hung upon 'this one fellow came to sojourn' — they said: you do not have the status of a resident, in whose hand it is to change the statutes according to the need of the hour; rather, you are a sojourner, and according to that understanding we accepted you to settle among us, on condition that you consent to all our statutes."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:28:48.010162791Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}